Vendored plugins from the Claude Code plugin directory, kept runnable.

Source:  https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official
Commit:  d182ca456ca09d31d139f7d3818d1d333b103cce
License: each plugin directory carries its own LICENSE file (Apache License
         2.0), vendored beside it unchanged.

Directories and their paths in the source repository:

  hookify/  <- plugins/hookify/

Every file is a byte-for-byte copy of the source at that commit, scripts
included, with the source's file modes: the suites push these directories as
a person would and run their hooks. upstream.json lists every file with its
git blob SHA and mode as the source's tree lists them at that commit, and
src/__tests__/real-plugins.test.ts proves the directories equal it, so the
proof that a plugin is unchanged needs no network. Anyone can repeat the
comparison against the source:

  gh api 'repos/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/git/trees/<commit>?recursive=1'

This NOTICE and upstream.json sit beside the plugin directories, never in
them, so an archive of a directory is exactly the published plugin. Nothing
under this directory is formatted, linted or edited; a change here is a
re-vendoring at a new commit and updates this notice and upstream.json.
